I couldn't see the body of `lateBy`, so I renamed the existing function to a private `lateDays` and put a new exported `lateBy` in front of it. The new one takes the day count from `lateDays` and returns the gap between `weekOf(job.dueDay + days)` and `weekOf(job.dueDay)`, never below 0. `weekOf` is the yard-week function the weekly summaries use. Which day gets measured and the always-0 cases stay inside `lateDays` untouched.

I'm assuming `lateDays` returns the plain difference between the measured day and `dueDay` when the job is late. If it caps or adjusts that number, the week count will be off. Also, if `weekOf` doesn't return a steadily increasing week number, the subtraction will need adjusting. Check the old body, and if it's a simple `day - dueDay`, I can fold it in properly and drop the helper.
